76/Castries_River_2019.jpg/960px-Castries_River_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cul de Sac River","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.983861,"lo":-61.011162,"d":3786,"ds":"The Cul De Sac River is a river in Castries Quarter of the island country of Saint Lucia. It flows north and then west from the central highlands in the south of the island, reaching the Caribbean Sea in Grand Cul de Sac Bay, south of the capital, Castries. It is one of the longest rivers in Saint Lucia.","wpu":"Cul de Sac River","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Cul_de_Sac_2010.jpg/960px-Cul_de_Sac_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Roseau Valley","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.953,"lo":-61.024,"d":7463,"ds":"The Roseau Valley is a second-order subdivision in the island nation of St. Lucia. It is home to the island's largest banana plantation.","wpu":"Roseau Valley","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Roseau_Valley2010.JPG/960px-Roseau_Valley2010.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pigeon Island (Saint Lucia)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.083333,"lo":-60.966667,"d":8320,"ds":"Pigeon Island is a 44-acre (180,000 m2) islet located in Gros Islet in the northern region of Saint Lucia. Once isolated from the country in the Caribbean Sea, the island was artificially joined to the western coast of mainland in 1972 by a man-made causeway built from dirt excavated to form the Rodney Bay Marina.","wpu":"Pigeon Island (Saint Lucia)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Pigeon_Island_historical_marker_for_Fort_Rodney.jpg/960px-Pigeon_Island_historical_marker_for_Fort_Rodney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Gros Islet","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.080833,"lo":-60.9525,"d":8716,"ds":"Gros Islet (English: Large Island) is a community near the northern tip of the island country of Saint Lucia, in the Gros Islet Quarter. Originally a quiet fishing village, it has become one of the more popular tourist destinations in the country.","wpu":"Gros Islet","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/At_the_top_of_Pigeon_Island.jpg/960px-At_the_top_of_Pigeon_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Anse La Raye","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.9459,"lo":-61.0369,"d":8837,"ds":"Anse La Raye or Anse-La-Raye is the largest town and seat of the Anse la Raye District of Saint Lucia. It is located on the island's western side, near Marigot Bay, and has several examples of French and English colonial architecture.","wpu":"Anse La Raye","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Anse_La_Raye_view.jpg/960px-Anse_La_Raye_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Castries ( ) is the capital and largest city of Saint Lucia, an island country in the Caribbean. The urban area has a population of approximately 20,000, while the eponymous district has a population of just under 70,000, as of May 2013. The city covers 80 km2 (31 sq mi).","wpu":"Castries","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/View_of_Castries_Saint_Lucia_Day248bdriveb.jpg/960px-View_of_Castries_Saint_Lucia_Day248bdriveb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}